{{!-- The publication's own menu, in the four shapes MIRROR's chrome needs.

This file is not called by name: `{{navigation}}` renders it, because Ghost's navigation
helper executes a partial called `navigation` if the theme ships one. What the helper hands
over is `navigation` — one entry per menu item with `label`, `url`, an optional `icon` and a
`current` flag it computes by comparing the item's path with the page's — plus, and this is
the load-bearing part, every extra attribute passed to the call (`_.merge(this, options.hash)`
in core/frontend/helpers/navigation.js). So `{{navigation variant="overlay"}}` arrives here as
`{{variant}}`, and one partial can serve the bar, the collapsed panel, a footer column and the
slim foot's row without the theme ever hardcoding a link.

Two consequences of that merge are worth knowing before adding a call:

1. It writes onto the calling context, so a `variant` set by one call would still be set
   for the next one. Every call therefore names its variant explicitly — there is no
   default branch to fall through to by accident.
2. The name has to be one no Ghost context uses. `title` would silently overwrite a post's
   title for the rest of the render, which is why the column heading is `heading`. --}}

{{!-- The bar and the overlay can open a submenu, so they render the menu as a tree — see
chrome/nav-tree.hbs. The footer's column and row are flat by design: the column lists top-level
items only and skips a `#` heading, because a "Parent / Child" label spelled out in the footer
and a link to nowhere are both worse than a submenu one hover away in the header. --}}
{{#match variant "bar"}}
	{{> "chrome/nav-tree"}}
{{/match}}

{{#match variant "overlay"}}
	{{> "chrome/nav-tree"}}
{{/match}}

{{#match variant "column"}}
	<nav aria-label="{{heading}}">
		<p class="text-muted mb-3.5 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{heading}}</p>
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-[9px]">
			{{#foreach navigation}}
				{{#match label "~" " / "}}{{else}}{{#match url "~$" "#"}}{{else}}
				<a
					href="{{url}}"
					class="font-ui text-text hover:text-accent text-sm no-underline">{{> "chrome/nav-label" iconSize="h-[14px]"}}</a>
				{{/match}}{{/match}}
			{{/foreach}}
		</div>
	</nav>
{{/match}}

{{#match variant "row"}}
	{{#foreach navigation}}
		<a
			href="{{url}}"
			class="font-ui text-text hover:text-accent text-[13.5px] no-underline">{{> "chrome/nav-label" iconSize="h-[13px]"}}</a>
	{{/foreach}}
{{/match}}
